      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} -2 = y^{3} - y^{2}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nRearranging once, test whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\nf(c) = c^{3} - c^{2} + 2\n$$\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=-4 + 2 + 8 \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=-1 - 1 + 2 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=0 + 0 + 2 \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$.",
